00:00:13.686 --> 00:00:15.202
Peewoop!

00:00:15.202 --> 00:00:16.140
(knuckles cracking)

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:19.387
Most knuckles cracked in 30 seconds.

00:00:19.387 --> 00:00:20.220
I feel like this

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.520
is my morning routine
right here. (chuckles)

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:23.850
Caught on camera, Dr.
Mike's morning routine.

00:00:23.850 --> 00:00:25.512
I feel like I could beat this one.

00:00:25.512 --> 00:00:28.345
(joints cracking)

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:33.816
Oh, cramp in the hamstring!
Cramp in the hamstring!

00:00:33.816 --> 00:00:34.649
(screen beeps)

00:00:34.649 --> 00:00:35.782
(light music)

00:00:35.782 --> 00:00:38.965
(man whistles)

00:00:38.965 --> 00:00:42.215
(woman sings low note)

00:00:43.487 --> 00:00:46.290
Vocal chords are obviously
what give you the ability

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:47.800
to speak and produce sound.

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:49.240
The larynx is a muscle.

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:51.180
By being able to control that muscle,

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:53.750
whether you're stretching
it out, you shortening it,

00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:56.700
you actually change your
ability to control your pitch.

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:59.110
And just like any other muscle,
this muscle can be trained.

00:00:59.110 --> 00:01:00.480
That's why we have vocal coaches.

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:01.536
- [Sam] See how low you can get.

00:01:01.536 --> 00:01:04.930
(Dr. Mike inhales)

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:05.763
- Was that low?

00:01:05.763 --> 00:01:06.612
- [Sam] I heard nothing.

00:01:06.612 --> 00:01:07.445
(both laugh)

00:01:07.445 --> 00:01:08.278
It was totally silent.

00:01:08.278 --> 00:01:09.263
- Exactly, it was that low.

00:01:09.263 --> 00:01:10.884
(Dr. Mike sings low note)

00:01:10.884 --> 00:01:12.100
(both laugh)
(screen beeps)

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:13.410
What do we got here?

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:15.083
Is this an age-related one?

00:01:16.538 --> 00:01:20.260
Wow. 116 as of March.

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:21.640
Is this person still live, Sam?

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:22.970
- [Sam] Yes, she is still alive.

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:26.210
- Wow. So two years older,
three years older, basically.

00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:27.240
Oh, birthday's coming up.

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:30.610
So gonna be a solid 119 in a few days.

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:32.803
Happy early birthday, Kane Tanaka.

00:01:32.803 --> 00:01:34.700
(serene piano music)
(people clapping)

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:36.365
Do you think she knows?

00:01:36.365 --> 00:01:37.300
(woman speaking japanese)

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:38.160
Yep. There you go.

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:39.940
She goes, "I don't know what this is."

00:01:39.940 --> 00:01:41.930
- My name is Nicholas James Stoeberl,

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:44.127
and I have the longest
tongue in recorded history.

00:01:44.127 --> 00:01:44.969
- Wow.

00:01:44.969 --> 00:01:46.700
- I think one of the most useful things

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:48.820
that my tongue offers
is actually not having

00:01:48.820 --> 00:01:49.653
to use a napkin.

00:01:49.653 --> 00:01:52.200
- Must be popular with his partners.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:53.759
- I use my tongue, actually,

00:01:53.759 --> 00:01:56.110
to create, you could call it, art.

00:01:56.110 --> 00:01:58.613
I sort of like to paint
on canvas using acrylic.

00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:01.450
- Everyone's got their thing.

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:03.950
He paints with his
tongue that's very long.

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:05.320
That's the longest tongue in the world.

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:06.930
I'm sure other people
would be doing other things

00:02:06.930 --> 00:02:08.320
with that tongue, but maybe it wasn't safe

00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:10.217
for Guinness World Records
to investigate further.

00:02:10.217 --> 00:02:11.050
(screen beeps)

00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:12.630
(man groans)

00:02:12.630 --> 00:02:16.100
What? The longest time in
an abdominal plank position.

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:18.610
Okay, here, we're talking
isometric contraction.

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:21.400
We're literally not shortening,
not lengthening the fibers,

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:24.360
but keeping them tight and
engaged the entire time.

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:25.200
- [Sam] Before you keep watching,

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:27.120
what's your prediction
for the longest plank?

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:30.290
- I'm gonna say something
wild. Five hours.

00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:32.330
In February, 2020, George Hood planked

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:35.170
for an astonishing 8 hours 15 minutes!

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:36.660
Does he have a catheter in place?

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:40.000
