00:07:52.220 --> 00:07:54.780
- I'm Cathie Jung, and I am currently

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:58.220
in the Guinness book
for the smallest waist

00:07:58.220 --> 00:07:59.593
on a living person.

00:08:02.030 --> 00:08:04.440
- This is very not
recommended and unhealthy.

00:08:04.440 --> 00:08:06.790
A few things happen when you
wear a waist trainer like that.

00:08:06.790 --> 00:08:10.020
One, you start actually
weakening your core muscles

00:08:10.020 --> 00:08:12.600
because you're not allowing
them to expand properly

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:13.620
and function properly.

00:08:13.620 --> 00:08:16.250
Second, you're also
cramming your intestines

00:08:16.250 --> 00:08:18.230
from properly performing peristalsis,

00:08:18.230 --> 00:08:20.890
which is that movement of
food throughout your body.

00:08:20.890 --> 00:08:23.100
Then you're also affecting
your breathing because

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:25.700
in order to breathe, your
ribs need to expand properly

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:27.260
and your diaphragm needs to lower.

00:08:27.260 --> 00:08:28.730
That's why we talk about belly breathing.

00:08:28.730 --> 00:08:30.310
So when you shallow breathe like that,

00:08:30.310 --> 00:08:33.050
you actually lose a part of your lungs

00:08:33.050 --> 00:08:35.140
through a condition known as atelectasis.

00:08:35.140 --> 00:08:36.610
But also it's short-lived.

00:08:36.610 --> 00:08:37.860
If you stop wearing the corsets,

00:08:37.860 --> 00:08:39.140
it'll return back to normal.

00:08:39.140 --> 00:08:40.040
And thank God for that.

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:42.110
The human body wants to
return back to normal.

00:08:42.110 --> 00:08:47.110
- Sultan Kosen, 8'1", 246
and a half centimeters.

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:48.830
Confirmed as the Guinness World Record's

00:08:48.830 --> 00:08:49.987
world's tallest man.

00:08:49.987 --> 00:08:52.280
- He has a pituitary tumor secreting

00:08:52.280 --> 00:08:53.720
a hormone called growth hormone.

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:54.690
- The pituitary gland

00:08:54.690 --> 00:08:56.490
is sometimes known as the master gland,

00:08:56.490 --> 00:08:58.368
'cause it secretes some of
the most important hormones

00:08:58.368 --> 00:09:01.070
that actually end up regulating,
sometimes, other hormones.

00:09:01.070 --> 00:09:04.420
Sometimes you can have a tumor
grow in the pituitary gland,

00:09:04.420 --> 00:09:06.110
which is actually not cancerous,

00:09:06.110 --> 00:09:09.640
but it is one that produces
more of a certain hormone.

00:09:09.640 --> 00:09:12.320
Also melanocytes, which secrete melanin,

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:14.830
the cells that give your skin pigment,

00:09:14.830 --> 00:09:18.340
actually are controlled by
melanocyte stimulating hormone,

00:09:18.340 --> 00:09:20.870
which is also found in
your pituitary gland.

00:09:20.870 --> 00:09:22.730
